WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.887
Then run the assessment
and keep the evidence.

2
00:00:02.887 --> 00:00:06.901
Five things are decided before either
tool touches a production tenant.

3
00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:11.350
Scope comes from the BOD
25-01 tenant inventory.

4
00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:15.728
The host is a dedicated Windows machine
inside the authorization boundary,

5
00:00:15.728 --> 00:00:19.550
a separate one for each tool,
because their dependencies conflict.

6
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:24.175
Each tool gets a reader account, with
consent granted once, separately.

7
00:00:24.175 --> 00:00:26.463
Output is handled as controlled data.

8
00:00:26.463 --> 00:00:31.933
And the assessment accounts belong
in the M-26-14 Agency Logging Plan,

9
00:00:31.933 --> 00:00:36.637
due 90 days after CISA's August
20 reference architecture.

10
00:00:36.637 --> 00:00:40.188
ScubaGear runs in Windows PowerShell 5.1.

11
00:00:40.188 --> 00:00:45.083
Its configuration file is the exception
record: annotations, omissions with

12
00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:49.825
a rationale and an expiration date,
and exclusions for emergency accounts.

13
00:00:49.825 --> 00:00:51.859
It's versioned in the repository,

14
00:00:51.859 --> 00:00:55.625
and its hash is recorded with
every run, like the tool version.

15
00:00:55.625 --> 00:01:00.700
The results file is never renamed
or edited, only hashed and copied.

16
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:05.975
The Zero Trust Assessment needs PowerShell
7 and can take more than 24 hours.

17
00:01:05.975 --> 00:01:10.370
And install the program's toolkit
only from its own repository:

18
00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:14.570
a package named fmp on the public
Python index is unrelated.
